{
  "_doc": "Drafts in an open thread (shared/src/thread-drafts.ts, Android :core ThreadDrafts.kt). `entries`: threadEntries(messages, local, outbox), `outbox` (absent: none) the Gmail message ids of drafts the Outbox holds: those show nowhere, Gmail's copy or the device's, unless the device holds the draft as sending. `messages` are Gmail's, oldest first, as {id, draft}; `local` are the device's drafts of the thread as {localId, messageId, state, updatedAt}, state one of draft, deleted, sending. `expect` lists what shows, in order: {kind: message|draft, id} for Gmail's copy, {kind: local, localId, sending} for the device's. `snippet`: draftSnippet(markdown), a draft's first words as plain text (at most 200 characters). `opening`: draftsOpening(inDrafts, event, openBefore, openAfter), the thread whose draft opens in the composer in place of the thread a list step opened (`event` the step's type, open before and after it, null for none): in Drafts only, only for a tap or Enter on a row, and only when it opened a thread not open before; `expect` null when the thread opens as usual. `held`: heldDraftStates({kept, thrown, sending}), the drafts this device holds and where each stands: `kept` the device's records as {localId, deleted} (deleted: a delete waiting for Gmail), `thrown` the ids thrown away here (undo window, or delete not done), `sending` the ids being sent here; `expect` lists {localId, state, kept}, kept records first in order, then the rest (thrown before sending), each once. A draft with no kept record is only ever deleted or sending, never a draft, so it can't be listed or opened.",
